set gridiron_kit

# The player holding the ball. Baking this as a composition means the ball is
# skinned to the arm and moves with it through every frame, and — the thing a
# separately drawn sprite cannot do — is correctly hidden behind the body when
# the player is facing away.

models
  body gridiron.wam
  ball football.wam

# One composition covers every clip. The ball sits in the right hand, and the
# animations do the rest: the same graft reads as a ball cocked beside the
# helmet through the throw and as one carried at the hip through the run,
# because the arm is in a different place in each.
#
# A tuck against the ribs was tried first and abandoned. Grafting to the
# forearm put both ends of the ball equally near the torso, so `hold`'s
# points-away check fired on every forward-facing orientation, and clearing
# the 0.03-0.05 body overlap meant guessing bone-space offsets that rotate
# with the bone — the hand-derived transform the language exists to avoid.
#
# The aim is stated rather than left to `hold`: the ball's declared carry
# leans toward `fwd` and the hand bone itself points forward, which is
# parallel and says nothing about which way to tilt.
compose carry
  base body
  # `overlap` because a fist closing on a ball necessarily intersects it: the
  # hand is a plain loft with no modelled fingers, so there is no placement
  # that both looks held and stays clear. The reported depth is checked below
  # rather than left unbounded.
  graft ball to=hand.r:0.45 align=grip aim=68:up scale=0.22 overlap

checks
  # The ball is deliberately larger than scale so it reads at sprite size: a
  # real one is 0.15 of a player's height and would be about six pixels here.
  # The game's own drawn ball was exaggerated the same way.
  # Measured on the COMPOSED ball, not the standalone model: length() on the
  # bare model returns its 0.17m girth, since its long axis is vertical in its
  # own space, which is not the number this is about.
  assert height(carry.ball.shell) / height(body) in 0.16..0.26
  # The ball may sink into the gripping arm, but only shallowly — deeper and
  # it is buried in the limb rather than held by it.
  assert clip(carry.ball.shell, carry.body.arm.r) < 0.06
  measure ballVsPlayer height(carry.ball.shell) / height(body)

every
  assert tris < 4000
